+Concise Bounded Description
+--------------------------
+
+The Concise Bounded Description (CBD) of a resource is the subgraph
+describing it, as defined in the `W3C member submission
+<https://www.w3.org/Submission/CBD/>`_. Use
+:meth:`~rdflib.graph.Graph.cbd` to extract it::
+
+   >>> from rdflib import Graph, BNode, Literal, Namespace
+   >>> EX = Namespace("http://example.org/")
+   >>> g = Graph()
+   >>> g.add((EX.bob, EX.name, Literal("Bob")))
+   >>> addr = BNode()
+   >>> g.add((EX.bob, EX.address, addr))
+   >>> g.add((addr, EX.city, Literal("Paris")))
+   >>> g.add((EX.alice, EX.name, Literal("Alice")))
+
+   >>> cbd = g.cbd(EX.bob)
+   >>> len(cbd)
+   3
+
+The result contains every triple whose subject is the resource. Whenever
+an object is a blank node, its own triples are included too, recursively.
+URI objects are not followed, so triples about ``EX.alice`` above are
+excluded. The source graph is left unchanged.
+
 Parsing data from a string
